      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5b0193bc0343a037142c1bf1",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Unless you are using different shaders on parts of your avatar, or have props (that will be separate meshes anyway), you do NOT need more than one material. Ever.\n\nIf you don't want to atlas you can just stitch textures and move the UVs.\n\nThe max material count should be somewhere around 5-10, with warnings above 3.\n\nEvery one of my avatars are one drawcall while maintaining their original quality. There is no excuse.\n\nI do not understand why your suggestion has not been implemented when we have word from the VRChat team that polygon count does not really affect performance and material count does. Whether that's correct or not I am unsure but this is what the team themselves claim.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
